--! A test platform's one capability: make Node look like a browser to
--! core's scheduler, which then escapes to a macrotask the way it does in a
--! page — through a `MessageChannel`, since a browser has no
--! `setImmediate`.

--| Remove `setImmediate`. A `MessageChannel` made afterwards does not keep
--| Node running by itself, as nothing a page holds keeps a page open.
pub foreign impure withoutImmediate : () → ()
